# ic-praxis: keep PERSONAL agent files out of a SHARED repo.
#
# `.claude/` is committed so the team shares rules, skills and commands — but a
# few things under it are per-person, not team assets. Without these lines a
# stray `git add -A` pushes someone's private notes into the team repo.
#
# Naming convention (see .claude/README.md): a personal memory file is
# `user-*.md` or `*.local.md`; anything else under .claude/memory/ is team
# knowledge and IS committed.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/memory/user-*.md
.claude/memory/*.local.md

# Backups left by ic-praxis <= v0.5.3's setup-claude-memory.sh (removed in
# v0.6.0). Restore yours with: bash scripts/unlink-claude-memory.sh
memory.bak.*
